<title>UK: UK March gas output falls on mild weather - WoodMa.</title>
<headline>UK March gas output falls on mild weather - WoodMa.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-05-02</dateline>
<text>
<p>UK gas production fell by 14.6 percent from February to March, with output down to 9,982 million cubic feet a day (mmcfd) from 11,687 mmcfd in February, consultants Wood Mackenzie said in their May North Sea Report.</p>
<p>Production was driven down by unseasonally mild weather, with output down by 868 mmcfd in comparison with March 1996, when higher demand was driven by colder weather.</p>
<p>The reduced demand was shown at the Morecambe fields, where production was down 36 percent to 1,178 mmcfd from February's average. And as seasonal demand changed, the Sdean field, used for peak shaving, produced no gas at all. Output from Rough storage was also off, to an average 38 mmcfd from February's 213 mmcfd.</p>
